1
00:00:00,133 --> 00:00:01,742
Croesus had a choice.

2
00:00:02,585 --> 00:00:05,822
Wait for Persia to grow
stronger or strike first.

3
00:00:06,502 --> 00:00:10,862
But Croesus was not a man who liked
leaving important decisions to chance.

4
00:00:11,942 --> 00:00:17,242
Years earlier, according to Herodotus, the
Athenian statesman Solon had visited him.

5
00:00:17,822 --> 00:00:19,682
Croesus showed him his immense wealth and

6
00:00:19,682 --> 00:00:22,622
expected to be called
the happiest man alive.

7
00:00:23,182 --> 00:00:24,602
Solon refused.

8
00:00:24,622 --> 00:00:26,082
His warning was simple.

9
00:00:26,082 --> 00:00:30,122
A man's fortune cannot truly be
judged until the end of his life.

10
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:34,042
Croesus did not know how important
those words would become.
